Z||000000||FieroMaster88||12-03-2000||08:50 PM||||Ok, you guys seem to know about Fiero's, how about giving me some advice? I have an 84 Indy Fiero. It is in rough shape, well, at least the interior is.  To start with, the back window was used for target practice by some punck little kids with bb guns, all the leather needs to be re-wraped, the red parts on the seats have cigarette burns, the dash is cracked all over the place, the steering column has about 6" of play in any direction and the back window is blown out! The body needs cleaning (big time) and the front facia is cracked.<BR>The good parts are that the frame is solid and that the car runs like new. I need to decide what to do with it. If I am gonna restore it, i will need to find some Interior parts for a good deal, or should I just sell it for scrap. Please give me an Idea of what to do!?!?!?!<P>Thanks,<P>James<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||LAMBO||12-03-2000||08:59 PM||||Every interior part you mentioned is replaceable and not too hard to find on the Internet. Is it your intention to restore  back to original, or just make it nice again? Just making it nice again makes it a little easier on the seats. Finding original style Indy seats in good to excellent shape may be your hardest task. Check with Fiero Dave or Indy Resto Guy on this forum. If they don't have the parts you need, they'll know where to get them. Good luck on your Indy, you'll enjoy it when your done. I know I do mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>TL<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indypost_1.JPG"> <p>[This message has been edited by LAMBO (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
